fore committing. Worktree wt/<id> kept (some have partial uncommitted edits) as salvage evidence; do NOT reap unless ahead>0+clean+content-identical.","worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"worker_status":"pending","dispatched_at":null}
 {"status":"pending","id":"DOC-5","title":"README Quick Start: _index.json entry count wrong and the documented --generate step dirties a tracked file","detail":{"fingerprint":"e2cdaf0baafb4f35fc1d5737de9bb6eecc4777d254e370e351db7e17276ef587"},"priority":"P4","source":null,"reasoning":"Rot + a downstream trap. README.md:285-294 (Quick Start, \"Verify Everything Works\") says: \"The spec index (_index.json) is regenerated by the test suite; it currently holds 466 entries (verified 2026-08-13). The generator is explicit-mode only: a bare `python3 scripts/generate_index.py` prints usage and exits without writing anything. Use `--generate` to (re)write the index\".\nLive reality (measured this tick):\n- `python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('/home/kara/speclang/_index.json'));print(len(d['specs']))\"` -> 464 entries, and the file's own `generated` field says \"2026-07-29T01:49:45.520ZZ\" - the README's \"466 (verified 2026-08-13)\" matches neither, and the file has not been regenerated since 2026-07-29 (git log -1 -- _index.json -> d4dd1b2c \"style: prettier format\").\n- The 466 number only appears when the generator runs over the live tree: `python3 scripts/generate_index.py --generate` output was \"Found 475 spec files / Created _index.json / - Specs: 466 / - References: 1263\". So the README quotes the generator's number while the committed file holds 464 - the committed artifact (what a reader actually opens) disagrees with the doc.\n- TRAP: that same documented command is a WRITE, not a check, and the README presents it under \"Verify Everything Works\" next to read-only steps. Running it modified the TRACKED file: `git diff --stat _index.json` -> 1 file changed, 16346 insertions(+), 10904 deletions(-) (475 files found vs 447 tracked .spec.md / 449 incl .scl, i.e. it swept untracked scratch spec copies). The foreman had to `git checkout -- _index.json` to undo it. Any contributor following Quick Start verbatim lands a 27k-line diff they did not intend.\nARTIFACT: README.md Quick Start step 4 (README.md:284-295).\nACCEPT: README states the entry count that the COMMITTED _index.json holds (or the file is regenerated in the same commit so the two agree), and the step is labelled as a write that dirties a tracked file, with the read-only alternative (`--validate`/`--tree`/`--impact`/`--graph`) named as the actual verification path.","ts":null,"complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-27T01:15:30.578947+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T19:15:00.000000+00:00","acceptance":"Two checks from repo root: (1) `python3 scripts/generate_index.py --generate --output /tmp/index-check.json` exits 0 and `python3 -c \"import json;a=json.load(open('/tmp/index-check.json'))['specs'];b=json.load(open('_index.json'))['specs'];print('OK' if a==b else 'FAIL')\"` prints OK, so regenerating leaves `git status --porcelain _index.json` empty (the documented step no longer dirties a tracked file); (2) `python3 -c \"import json,re;n=len(json.load(open('_index.json'))['specs']);m=[int(x) for x in re.findall(r'(\\d+) entries',open('README.md').read())];print('OK %d'%n if m and all(v==n for v in m) else 'FAIL %s'%m)\"` prints 'OK 464' \u2014 the Quick Start entry count matches the real index.","foreman_note":"Doc-severity re-triage 2026-11-03 (readme audit lane, tick speclang-readme-2026-11-03-15-46-12) per Bane ruling 2026-09-30: documentation findings are P4 (P5 for polish), never P1-P3. POLICY change only, not a new assessment \u2014 the finding is unchanged and still reproduces on the published tip 4cb5bbfb (README.md:287 '466 entries' vs committed _index.json).\n\n2026-11-16 tick 23-53: reset from in_progress \u2014 sibling wave worker for this row died without committing any code (worktree wt/* at base, no commits; main-tree diff absent for docs rows). Shared-checkout recovery by foreman tick speclang-foreman-2026-11-16-23-53-17: sibling wave SpecLang-dogfood-2026-11-16-22-47-48 workers were killed before committing. Worktree wt/<id> kept (some have par